 "note": "RPCS3 Core 921 = Core 920 plus the release of stale idle textures, for the memory of Call of Duty: Black Ops II and every title. REWINDBOX_STALE_TEXTURE_SWEEP_921: on iOS every CPU texture is confirmed by a hash of its guest bytes, never by page protection, so a texture whose memory the title reused stayed cached until looked up again and upstream trim_sections only visits blocks of more than 256 locked sections (Black Ops II, builds 620-721: texture pool 74 -> 568 MiB in 4.4 minutes, none released); once per presented frame a pass bounded to 4 MiB hashed and 2048 sections looked at releases the idle, unbound hash-validated CPU textures whose bytes no longer match, exactly as their next lookup would; intact ones are kept. Setting Stale texture release, Automatic = every title; COREPROF TEXSWEEP921. Core 920 (pinned f9f2b478): no lever alternation in ordinary play, ZCULL cost line. No resolution, precision, frame limit, SPU count or priority or LLVM option changes. No codegen input changes: identities unchanged. Host bridge 8977315e unchanged; MoltenVK dependency of run 42733987255 (library d19d3a42). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 42872597093, attempt 1, source 03a52515; Apple host harnesses run 42872597093 on 03a52515). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle). Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
